{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nDocumentation-only Gerrit changes currently consume the complete OS/Python matrix plus mutation, packaging, optionality, identity, eval, and golden-path jobs. The operator approved a reduced lane only when trusted classification proves every changed path is documentary. Python, shell, workflows/actions, dependencies/locks, builds, tests/fixtures, configuration/policy, unknown paths, and unavailable diffs always select full Verify. Docs-only Verify retains every documentation-related generated-doc, drift, index, cross-reference, quickstart, and reference-validation gate.\n\n## Trust and diff contract\nThe routing decision controls Verified and therefore runs only from trusted `origin/main`, mirroring the existing trusted-main vote normalizer. The routing job checks out the exact patchset as data and separately sparse-checks out the classifier plus complete allowlist from `origin/main` with credentials disabled. It never imports, sources, or executes patchset-controlled classifier logic or configuration. The exact change set is `HEAD^..HEAD`; the job explicitly deepens the mirror-first checkout until `HEAD^` resolves, using the existing dependency-audit pattern. A normally completing classifier emits `route=full` for parent-resolution failure, an empty or malformed path list, or any non-allowlisted path. If the classifier job itself fails or is cancelled before emitting an output, every full-route job uses `always() && (needs.classifier.result != 'success' || needs.classifier.outputs.route == 'full')` and therefore still runs; the docs-only job requires classifier success plus `route=docs-only` and cannot run. The failed classifier result remains in `vote.needs` and blocks Verified even when fallback full jobs pass.\n\nNative GitHub `paths:` and patchset-local filtering are rejected because this workflow is Gerrit `workflow_dispatch` and the security-sensitive decision must not come from the untrusted patchset tree. The new classifier may reuse the existing `dependency_audit.changed_files` parsing seam from trusted main if its error contract fits; otherwise it must preserve the same fail-closed semantics.\n\n## Shared documentation gates\nInventory the current inline gates and extract only the documentation-relevant steps into `.github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml`. Both callers first perform their already-required checkout and Python/uv setup, then invoke the same composite action. The action does not own checkout. This form avoids adding a new runner/job to the full lane while single-sourcing gate commands; a separate reusable-workflow job was rejected because it would increase full-lane runner usage, contrary to the contention constraint. Inline copies are removed.\n\nPreflight and migrate every structural consumer that reads `_build-and-test.yml`: `test_gate_step_tree_skew.py`, `test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, `test_check_adr_numbers_heldout.py`, `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py`, `test_complexity_baseline.py`, `test_extra_coverage_guard.py`, `test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew.py`, `test_dependency_advisory_wiring.py`, and `test_worktree_python_pin.py`. Each affected invariant must follow the extracted action rather than be weakened or deleted; consumers of gates that remain inline stay unchanged.\n\n## Routing and aggregation\n- Add an unconditional trusted classifier job after clear-vote and ticket resolution.\n- A proven docs-only patchset runs one Ubuntu docs-only job that invokes the shared action.\n- Full build/test, mutation, optionality, artifact, eval, golden-path, and identity jobs run only on the full route.\n- Add classifier and docs-only results to `vote.needs`; make normalization route-aware so exactly one route must execute and skipped jobs from the other route are neutral. A classifier-job failure runs the full fallback route and also blocks Verified. A missing lane, executed-job failure, or docs-gate failure blocks Verified.\n- Update `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` and its tests so the docs-only gate cannot be omitted from vote aggregation.\n- Create parameterized `tests/scripts/test_classify_gerrit_verify_change.py` cases for every documented path category, exact `HEAD^..HEAD` parent handling, malformed/empty input, classifier exceptions, and the successful docs-only control; gate them with `python -m pytest tests/scripts/test_classify_gerrit_verify_change.py`.\n- Preserve clear-vote, resolvable-ticket, secret, and vote-key boundaries.\n- Document the allowlist rationale, fail-closed rule, and safe extension process in `CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n- Measure the first genuine docs-only run against change 1778 / run 31817494677. Back-out is a Gerrit revert restoring unconditional full Verify.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Allowlisted documentation-only paths select the docs-only route.\n- [ ] Any Python path selects full Verify.\n- [ ] Any shell or executable path selects full Verify.\n- [ ] Any workflow or action path selects full Verify.\n- [ ] Any dependency or lockfile path selects full Verify.\n- [ ] Any test or fixture path selects full Verify.\n- [ ] Any repository configuration or policy path selects full Verify.\n- [ ] Any unrecognized path selects full Verify.\n- [ ] An empty, malformed, unreadable, or parentless diff selects full Verify.\n- [ ] Classifier logic and the complete allowlist execute only from trusted `origin/main`.\n- [ ] A patchset modifying routing logic, workflow, or action cannot select docs-only Verify.\n- [ ] Documentation gates have one extracted definition and no copied command list.\n- [ ] The shared gate retains ADR number, index, and cross-reference validation.\n- [ ] The shared gate retains docs-index and README quickstart validation.\n- [ ] The shared gate retains CLI, MCP, and env-registry drift validation.\n- [ ] The inventory test retains every other current documentation-related guard.\n- [ ] Existing workflow-structure tests follow extracted gates without losing assertions.\n- [ ] Docs-only Verify skips the OS/Python matrix and mutation.\n- [ ] Docs-only Verify skips optionality, artifact, eval, golden-path, and identity jobs.\n- [ ] Full Verify uses no additional runner job for documentation gates.\n- [ ] The resolvable-ticket and clear-vote gates remain unconditional.\n- [ ] `vote.needs` includes every route result required for fail-closed Verified.\n- [ ] A classifier job failure still runs every full-route job.\n- [ ] A classifier job failure cannot yield Verified +1.\n- [ ] A failed documentation gate cannot yield Verified +1.\n- [ ] Workflow policy tests, lint, and typecheck pass.\n- [ ] `CONTRIBUTING.md` explains the docs-only allowlist contract and safe extension rule.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Gerrit LLM-Review reaches +1; record change, patchset, vote, and timestamp.\n  provenance: environment=production Gerrit; principal=rebar-review-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the production review bot vote is the contract.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Gerrit Verified reaches +1; record change, workflow run, patchset, vote, and timestamp.\n  provenance: environment=production GitHub Actions and Gerrit; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the production CI vote exercises the deployed workflow.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The merged SHA and merge timestamp are recorded before closure.\n  provenance: environment=production Gerrit; principal=authenticated submitter; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Gerrit merge state is authoritative.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Genuine docs-only wall clock and runner-minutes are compared with run 31817494677.\n  provenance: environment=production GitHub Actions; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — production job timestamps and conclusions provide the measurement."}},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786725386937053001,"uuid":"d0e576d0-1ccc-41e9-a664-6c788190488e"}